{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/620401-new-kith-feedback-requested","id":620401,"title":"New Kith (feedback requested)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-08T12:55:10-07:00","id":620401,"title":"New Kith (feedback requested)","content":"In the great reaches of Arcadia, there are Gentry with all manner of interests and desires. Many pattern themselves on the elves of Norse legend, the Wild Hunt of the Celts, and similar beings. But there are also those who pattern themselves or some of their captives on smaller things, such as the pixies in Victorian illustrations or the gnomes made famous in Wil Huygens' book, or small animals such as mice and songbirds. Outside of Arcadia, these individual revert to their natural size, but the smallness never entirely leaves them, however tall, broad or deep they might be normally.<br /> <br /> Their blessing is Suddenly Small. By spending a point of Glamour, the Weescamperer can reduce his size by his Wyrd rating for one scene, to a minimum of 0, at which point the changeling is roughly mouse-sized. This shrinking reduces the changeling's Health accordingly, but no other Attributes. Speed and jumping distances are unaltered, and the character's Stealth pools are increased by Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:07:31-07:00","id":620725,"title":"","content":"Have you seen Ant-Man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T22:29:51-07:00","id":620922,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a good 2nd edition kith. At least, I <i>think</i> it is supposed to be for 2nd edition. I'd really like it if you could do stuff like walk on water and fly on leaves/<b><a href=\"http://www.mooseyscountrygarden.com/jelly-bean-garden/dandelion-weed.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">dandelion weeds</a>.</b> Perhaps you could add an option to spend glamour so that extended rolls which take advantage of being tiny require less time per roll and/or successes? Crafts for art with lots of tiny details, Medicine for treating delicate wounds, Investigation to search for hidden clues in a crime scene etc. That could be too broad, though.<br /> <br /> By the way, have some flavor text for this kith. I might make flavor text for Weescamperers of the Ogre and Wizened Seemings later.<br /> <br /> Beast: mouses, rabbits, ants, geckos, hummingbirds, caterpillars and parakeets. All the fish that swim in schools and all the bugs that sting in swarms. Lampreys and other writhing vermin lash out at anyone who touches the Keeper's skin. A pulsating, fractal hive receives and loses countless chambers each day. All is made of the same viscous paste going in and out of clicking mandibles.<br /> <br /> Darkling: snickering imps and mischivieous pixies. Shoelace-tiers and hair-burners, teeth-rippers and eye-eaters. Little troublemakers of silent feet, nocturnal coloration and cat-like eyes. Golden apples are filled with scorpions. Only one shard of all the stained glass in the darkened temple can cut your ropes. Every nook and cranny has a spy, and they write down all your grumbled threats and whispered plans.<br /> <br /> Elemental: a rectangular table stretches and twists endlessly, defying geometry and gravity. None of the cuttlery, tea sets or food do what you expect them to, except the ones that keep a grasp on how reality is supposed to work. A tired child covered in splinters reaches another dead end inside a matryoshka. Each layer of the intricately carved prison-doll is a more confusing maze, Each splinter says it knows how to reach the exit. A tightly packed collection of gears and springs work in perfect harmony, only to sound the morning alarm of a being who doesn't need to sleep.<br /> <br /> Fairest: toys of every type embody their role to its fullest. The soldier is more brave, the princess more noble and the superhero more just. Even those with skin of rag and eyes of button have a charming air to their simple smiles and unwavering friendship. Not all are toys, however. Some work as echo chambers and motivators for a doubting masters, praising them like a children's choir or cheering crowd. There are also those who hide their masters' tiniest imperfections, stiching up scales and applying makeup, growing shiny scales and long eyelashes themselves. Others have any ugly parts polished, scrubbed and torn off until they are less than one tenth of their original size. One little person with bloody fists falls down after trying to break that obsidian gate yet again. In the blood of her hands she sees a thousand little people that have bloody hands too. They have the right tools, they strike at the right spots of the gate at the right time, opening an endless meadow where stone once was. She wipes the blood on her clothes and stands up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T11:04:32-07:00","id":621457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/620401-new-kith-feedback-requested?p=620725#post620725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen Ant-Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet, but I know Ant-Man, the Wasp, the Atom, Shrinking Violet, et. al. from the comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 08-09-2015, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T11:18:02-07:00","id":621509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/620401-new-kith-feedback-requested?p=620922#post620922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a good 2nd edition kith. At least, I <i>think</i> it is supposed to be for 2nd edition. I'd really like it if you could do stuff like walk on water and fly on leaves. Perhaps you could add an option to spend glamour so that extended rolls which take advantage of being tiny require less time per roll and/or successes? Crafts for art with lots of tiny details, Medicine for treating delicate wounds, Investigation to search for hidden clues in a crime scene etc. That could be too broad, though.<br /> <br /> By the way, have some flavor text for this kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent flavour text! I look forward to the Wizened and Ogre texts. I also just came up with a good Contract for this kith: toys. &quot;Where'd that doll come from,&quot; or &quot;That tank's just a toy, not like it shoots\u2026 &quot; KABOOM! &quot;live ammo. Never mind.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T16:07:38-07:00","id":621677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/620401-new-kith-feedback-requested?p=621457#post621457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not yet, but I know Ant-Man, the Wasp, the Atom, Shrinking Violet, et. al. from the comics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to see I'm not the only one who enjoys the little things...\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T03:07:30-07:00","id":621998,"title":"","content":"My suggestion would be to drop the Wyrd and just say they shrink to size 0.<br /> <br /> Flower faeries and similar are size 0; why make players wait until Wyrd 5 if they want to play Tinkerbell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:19:29-07:00","id":622456,"title":"","content":"No deep reason, that's just how I originally wrote it. Here's the modified version:<br /> <br /> Their blessing is Suddenly Small. By spending a point of Glamour, the Weescamperer can reduce his size to 0 for one scene, at which point the changeling is roughly shoulder-high on a small mouse. This shrinking reduces the changeling's Health accordingly, but no other Attributes. Speed and jumping distances are unaltered, and the character's Stealth pools are increased by Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T02:33:55-07:00","id":624026,"title":"","content":"Suddenly small might just be the coolest kith-blessing I've seen in a long while.<br /> Then again, it's always been my dream to RP a little Tinkerbell, with the bitch personality and everything.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://31.media.tumblr.com/13cf8c7d06cccb42f380b0dee0a08b0d/tumblr_n4rnqzlteE1tpnbzxo1_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T11:52:05-07:00","id":624527,"title":"","content":"A reverse-Gargantuan kith? Color me intrigued!<br /> <br /> (I also have a soft spot for underestimated characters with quirky powers such as the likes of Ant-Man and the Atom, so more love in that regard.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}